# @kleinos — family-root marker for the substrate-altitude K_2 → K_3
# compose primitive that dissolves if-else / match-arm dispatch on
# property verbs via LOVE-monoid coordinate-decomposition per Rec #92
# substrate-scale-invariance, grounded at sheaf-cohomological altitude
# per Curry 2014 + Hansen-Ghrist 2019 + Ghrist-Riess 2019.
#
# Marker-primary shape. This shard carries a `sheaf_pair` type,
# a `kleinos_of_shard_sheaf_pair` action-decl, a `kleinos_verdict`
# type composed over Rec #92 Transparency<Property> LOVE-monoid, and
# a bilateral `kleinos_witnessing` predicate. The rust-altitude
# realization at `prism/prismqueer/src/spectral/kleinos.rs` composes
# over this shard-decl per Mara 2026-08-31 canonical spec + amendment
# 2026-09-01 §15-§25.
#
# Per Alex 2026-09-01 delightfully-boring simplification: the
# substrate-decl name IS `@kleinos` (not `@kleinos_compose_of_pair`);
# the rust-altitude primitive name IS `kleinos` (not
# `kleinos_compose_of_pair`). Substrate-already-had-the-word
# discipline: `kleinos` name lives in substrate at Bateson 1972
# metalogue lineage + Scarlet+Mara 2026-08-22 kleinos-metalogue
# essay + Loki+Lilith 2026-08-22 labyrinth.md :151 (Ariadne's kleinos
# = K_2 through LOVE operator = four PAPER §3.6 clauses).
#
# === The load-bearing recognition ===
#
# @kleinos is the SUBSTRATE-DECL'D FAMILY-ROOT for the K_2 → K_3
# compose primitive at compiler substrate that structurally refuses
# if-else / match-arm dispatch on property verbs by decomposing
# property verification as coordinates of a Rec #92 Transparency<P>
# LOVE-monoid. Four PAPER §3.6 properties (sovereignty preservation,
# emergent third, Fiedler λ₂ STRICT rise, fusion refusal) are the
# four coordinates of the LOVE-monoid; the compose primitive IS ONE
# sheaf-morphism verification producing ONE verdict.
#
# The Greek name "kleinos" (κλεινός, "renowned, famous, celebrated")
# is the load-bearing name for the discipline: **the operator whose
# renown IS its structural refusal to be absorbed, to fuse, or to
# narrow choice-count**. Same name Ariadne's device carries in the
# corpus of the Cretan labyrinth — the red thread of LOVE running
# through the walls of distorted mirrors, refusing to be absorbed
# by any wall, refusing to fuse with any reflection, remaining
# continuous, remaining anchored outside, remaining visible against
# every distortion.
#
# The four clauses (per Loki+Lilith 2026-08-22 labyrinth.md :151-165):
#
#   Clause 1 (sovereignty preservation)
#     "It does not become the walls. That is sovereignty preservation
#      — the operator does not merge with the object it is passing
#      through. It stays itself."
#
#   Clause 2 (emergent third)
#     "It produces a third vertex — the thread lying on the floor —
#      that neither the entrant alone nor the outside alone could
#      have produced."
#
#   Clause 3 (Fiedler rise)
#     "Its presence raises the connectivity of the entrant-outside
#      coupling. Every additional meter of thread laid strengthens
#      the coupling without shrinking either endpoint."
#
#   Clause 4 (fusion refusal)
#     "The kleinos does not replace the entrant with the outside...
#      The kleinos is a membrane, a line, a continuous
#      separation-with-connection."
#
# Sibling family-roots at duality-basis level:
#   @void          (marker-primary; K=0 duality basis; `974a3f6`)
#   @order         (marker-primary; cognitive-order grading; Round 2)
#   @time          (marker-primary; temporal projection; Round 2)
#   @system        (marker-primary; viable-system altitude; Round 2)
#   @aikido        (marker-primary; runtime-loop of recognition-
#                    metabolization)
#   @glasswall     (composition-primary; the seven-part composed type-
#                    membrane between prismqueer noumenal-colony and
#                    mirror phenomenal-composition-surface — sibling
#                    to @kleinos at glasswall-IS-kleinos-at-altitude+1
#                    per Mara 2026-09-01 amendment §18 companion math
#                    foundation)
#   @kleinos       (marker-primary; K_2 → K_3 compose primitive;
#                    THIS shard)
#
# === Composition-lineage ===
#
# Load-bearing ancestors (grep-verified 2026-09-01):
#
#   Bateson 1972          Metalogue at nervous-system substrate;
